<title>USA: USDA economist - '97 food inflation 2.5-3.0 pct.</title>
<headline>USDA economist - '97 food inflation 2.5-3.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department chief economist Keith Collins Monday said U.S. food prices will rise between 2.5 and 3.0 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>In a speech to USDA's annual Agricultural Outlook Forum, Collins said price increases would be restrained by meat and dairy product prices.</p>
<p>In 1996, food prices rose 3.3 percent above the 1995 level, the biggest one-year gain of the decade.</p>
</text>
